// Precedence: unary '-' vs '*'. Multiplication can't distinguish grouping
// here (negating one factor of a product is the same regardless of
// bracketing), so this checks the unary binds only to the immediately
// following primary, not further: -2 * 3 must be (-2) * 3 = -6, not
// -(2 * 3) [also -6, degenerate] and specifically NOT parsed as unary
// grabbing "2 * 3" as its argument in some other broken way that would
// reject the program or mis-scope a later term -- see
// precedence_unary_sub.dl for a case where the two groupings actually
// differ numerically.
.decl p(a:number)
.output p
p(X) :- X = -2 * 3.
